{"skill":{"slug":"amazon-competitor-analyzer","displayName":"Amazon Competitor Analyzer"},"version":{"version":"0.1.6","createdAt":1772008504998,"changelog":"- No changes detected in this version; all documentation and configurations remain the same as the previous release.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4060,"sha256":"daecda566786c6ba68a4ccdf17ce2cec8659d6944322d44ea46d58b12f97e543","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"amazon_competitor_analyzer.py","size":13770,"sha256":"401eab1ed0af8d97b82d5af730eafed6d32719273b9a57d9ca23cbb3ac7a21d6","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2162,"sha256":"de95d40a128b71fae09879109ddc265ff5bf257c243ecd78be599a9c7de26aec","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789037010502,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2e6a7f01685277d883c7e981a4e87e23756af4c675eba40ef8e0485b1fb76211","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2e6a7f01685277d883c7e981a4e87e23756af4c675eba40ef8e0485b1fb76211","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: amazon-competitor-analyzer\nVersion: 0.1.6\n\nThe skill's code and documentation are aligned with its stated purpose of scraping Amazon product data using the browseract.com API and generating competitive analysis reports. It correctly uses the `BROWSERACT_API_KEY` for authentication with the specified external service. There is no evidence of unauthorized data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent in the `SKILL.md` file. While the script allows writing output files to a user-specified directory, this is a standard feature for CLI tools and does not indicate malicious intent by the skill developer.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161866945},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789037010502},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent Amazon competitor-analysis tool, but users should know it sends ASINs to BrowserAct and writes local reports that may contain untrusted marketplace content.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to BrowserAct and use of BROWSERACT_API_KEY are proportionate to the purpose; automatic co-located .env loading and the --api-key CLI option are common but should be handled carefully.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, lifecycle hook, remote payload retrieval, or tool wrapping was found; setup is limited to documented Python package installation for requests and optional python-dotenv.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses BrowserAct use, the required API key, .env loading, output formats, and output directory, though third-party data handling and default file-writing behavior could be more prominent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No background persistence, privilege escalation, scheduled tasks, or system modification was found; persistence is limited to CSV, Markdown, and JSON reports written to the selected or default output directory.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The declared purpose is to scrape Amazon product data from user-provided ASINs via BrowserAct and generate competitive analysis; the Python code implements that workflow without unrelated capabilities.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, use this only with ASINs you are comfortable sending to BrowserAct. Prefer BROWSERACT_API_KEY via environment or a protected .env file instead of --api-key, keep the output directory intentional, and treat generated CSV files as untrusted when opening them in spreadsheet software.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The .env and environment-variable access is documented for the BrowserAct API key and is scoped to the skill directory; no credential harvesting beyond that purpose was found.\n[LP3] expected: The skill uses environment access, network requests, and file writes for its stated workflow, but clearer permission scoping would improve transparency.\n[SQP-2] expected: ASIN transmission to BrowserAct is central to the declared scraping workflow and BrowserAct is named in the skill text, though users would benefit from a clearer privacy notice.\n[SDI-2] expected: The code's .env loading matches the documented environment configuration instructions rather than a hidden local-data inspection behavior.\n[E1] expected: Requests to https://api.browseract.com/v2/workflow are necessary for the advertised BrowserAct automation workflow and no covert destination was identified.\n[TT2] expected: The returned task_id is reused only with the same BrowserAct workflow API to poll status and fetch results; validation could be tighter but this is consistent with the workflow.\n[SDI-1] expected: CSV, Markdown, and JSON report generation is described in the skill usage and parameters, though the code default writes to the current directory rather than the documented ./output default.\n[T09] unexpected: The CSV formula-injection risk and command-line API key exposure are real hardening issues, but they are implementation weaknesses rather than evidence of malicious intent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789037010502}}}}}